 r←eventNameOf event
⍝ The event NAME for an event number, or the argument unchanged if it is
⍝ already a name (or is a number nobody has a name for).
⍝
⍝ The inverse of eventNumber, and needed for the same reason: ⎕WC lets an
⍝ application use either form interchangeably. ('Event' 37 'DISPCARDS')
⍝ registers a callback, and `1 ⎕NQ obj 37 0 CARD` fires it — but registered
⍝ events are stored by name, so a numeric ⎕NQ matches nothing unless it is
⍝ resolved first.
⍝
⍝ That failure is silent: ∆NQ logs "No callback defined for event 37" and
⍝ returns, so the application simply does not do the thing it asked for. In
⍝ Arachnid it meant the Show Stack window drew no cards at all, because
⍝ DISPRESIZE primes the scrollbar with ⎕NQ and DISPCARDS -- which draws them --
⍝ only ever runs as that event's callback.
 r←event
 :If ~isChar event
 :AndIf (≢EVENTNUMS)≥EVENTNUMS⍳event
     r←(EVENTNUMS⍳event)⊃EVENTNAMES
 :EndIf
